+
+The choice of tier determines how much work is needed to retrieve this
+state. KV already in the executor's HBM is directly available to kernels;
+local DRAM requires host-to-device transfer, and remote DRAM also requires
+network transfer. With host staging, shared storage adds storage and
+network reads before the host-to-device transfer. Computation and
+prefetching can overlap some of this work, but retention still occupies
+capacity and transfers compete for bandwidth with foreground requests.
+Discarding the last reusable copy releases space at the cost of
+reconstruction on a later request or recovery. The serving system must
+therefore decide which histories to preserve and where, accounting for
+both future reuse and the effect of recovery on workflow completion.
 
